Handle Bedrock reasoningContent blocks (unblocks xAI Grok).

Reasoning models on Bedrock return a `reasoningContent` block alongside their text
/ toolUse blocks. xAI Grok 4.6 reasons by DEFAULT (effort low|medium|high|xhigh),
so it emits one on essentially EVERY response — including tool-calling turns.

goose's Bedrock formatter had no match arm for it, so every turn fell through to
the catch-all and killed the whole response:

  Execution error: Unsupported content block type from Bedrock

That makes Grok (and any other reasoning model on Bedrock) unusable through the
aws_bedrock provider, even though the Converse call itself succeeds — the failure
is purely in goose's response parsing.

Fix, both directions:

  * INBOUND (from_bedrock_content_block): map ReasoningContent -> the existing
    MessageContent::Thinking / RedactedThinking variants (goose already has these;
    the Anthropic formatter uses them). RedactedContent is kept as base64 rather
    than dropped. An unknown future reasoning variant is skipped, not fatal.

  * OUTBOUND (to_bedrock_message_content): replay a Thinking block that carries a
    signature as a reasoningContent block. Bedrock requires the reasoning text and
    its signature be passed back UNMODIFIED in a multi-turn conversation, so the
    previous behaviour (collapse to an empty text block) silently discarded the
    model's reasoning context on every subsequent turn. Thinking WITHOUT a
    signature did not come from Bedrock, so it keeps the old empty-text behaviour
    rather than sending something Bedrock would reject.

Upstream note: block/goose#6192 added reasoning_content to the OPENAI-compatible
formatter (DeepSeek-style APIs); the Bedrock Converse formatter was missed and
still carries a comment asserting "Bedrock doesn't use this format". Carry this as
a downstream cargoPatches patch until an upstream-fixed goose is pinned.
